# /root/.ssh/authorized_keys -- Avast Omni.
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO KEY IN THIS FILE. It is a header; the build appends
# the real key(s) to it.
#
# sshd here has PasswordAuthentication no (sshd_config.d/10-omni.conf) and the
# build locks root's password to '*', so whatever ends up in this file is the
# ONLY way into the box over the network. A key committed here would therefore
# mean every image anyone builds from this repository trusts one particular
# person and nobody else -- convenient for whoever committed it, a backdoor for
# everyone else, and useless to anyone who just wants to build the firmware.
#
# So the key is a build input:
#
#     ./rootfs/build-rootfs.sh --ssh-pubkey-file ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub ...
#     ./rootfs/build-rootfs.sh --ssh-pubkey 'ssh-ed25519 AAAA... you@host' ...
#     OMNI_SSH_PUBKEY='ssh-ed25519 AAAA... you@host' ./rootfs/build-rootfs.sh ...
#
# A build with no key fails, on purpose; check-image-invariants.sh fails on the
# finished image too. Pass --allow-no-ssh-key if you really do want an image
# reachable only over the serial console.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, rather than only /data/ssh/authorized_keys:
# sshd is configured with
#     AuthorizedKeysFile .ssh/authorized_keys /data/ssh/authorized_keys
# so keys can come from either place.
#
#   * THIS file is per-slot (it lives in the rootfs) and so guarantees access to
#     any slot that boots, even if /data is missing, unmounted or empty. /data is
#     nofail in fstab precisely so a bad p3 cannot stop the box booting -- which
#     would otherwise take SSH down with it.
#   * /data/ssh/authorized_keys is for keys added per-device after deployment;
#     those survive an A/B flip but depend on p3 mounting.
#
# Public keys only. Never put a private key in this repo -- the build refuses
# one, but do not rely on that.
